using "platforms/cpus/stm32f746.repl"

// STM32F746G-DISCO over the generic STM32F746 cpu description (platforms/cpus/stm32f746.repl):
//
//  - SRAM is 384 KiB there (64 KiB DTCM + 240 KiB SRAM1 + 16 KiB SRAM2), flash 2 MiB: both
//    cover the board (320 KiB SRAM, 1 MiB flash — the linker script only uses flash's first
//    MiB and the SRAM1+SRAM2 range at 0x20010000).
//
//  - The SDRAM (MT48LC4M32B2 on FMC bank 1) is plain mapped memory at 0xC0000000, which is
//    where the LTDC framebuffers live. There is no FMC register model, so the emulated build
//    skips BSP_SDRAM_Init (display.cpp) — the controller has nothing to configure.
//
//  - The board's HSE is 25 MHz (only used if the firmware configures clocks; the Renode build
//    skips SystemClock_Config, so the emulated CPU stays on the reset clock).
//
//  - The touch panel: FT5336 on I2C3 (the board's touch bus, PH7/PH8 AF4) at 7-bit address
//    0x38, reporting the RK043FN48H panel's 480x272. Its interrupt line is PI13 (TS_INT_PIN),
//    i.e. EXTI line 13 -> EXTI15_10_IRQn. The firmware polls the touch, so the line is not
//    needed, but wired anyway. With the GUI (run.resc), the mouse on the `showAnalyzer
//    sysbus.ltdc` window drives this model.
//    `isRotated` mirrors the real chip, which reports the panel's axes swapped (touch.cpp
//    swaps them back): with it set, MoveTo x y in a script means panel pixel (x, y).
touchscreen: Input.FT5336 @ i2c3 0x38
    MaxX: 480
    MaxY: 272
    isRotated: true
    -> gpioPortI@13
